209 - That Glorious Day Is Coming
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 209
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[C]That glorious day [Am/C]is [C]coming,
[C]The hour [F]is hastening [Em]on;
[E7/G#]Its [Am]radiant light is [Bm]nearing,
[Am/C]Far [G/D]brighter than the [Dm]sun;
[G7/F]In [C/E]yonder [Am]clouds of [Em/B]heaven,
[Dm]The [A/C#]Savior [C]will appear,
[C7/A#]And [F/A]gather [Am]all His [C/G]chosen,
[C/G]To [G7]meet Him in the [C]air.

Verse 2:
[C]The saints, then all [Am/C]victorious
[C]Will [F]go to meet [Dm/F]their [Em]Lord;
[E7/G#]An [Am]earth both bright and [Bm]glorious,
[Am/C]Will [G/D]then be their reward;
[G7/F]And [C/E]God [Em]Himself [Am]there [Em/B]reigning,
[Dm]Will [A/C#]wipe all [C]tears away;
[C7/A#]Nor [F/A]clouds nor [Am]night remaining,
[C/G]But [G7]one eternal [C]day.

Verse 3:
[C]O Christian, keep [Am/C]from [C]sleeping,
[C]And [F]let your love [Dm/F]abound;
[E7/G#]Be [Am]watchful, prayerful, [Bm]faithful,
[Am/C]The [G/D]trumpet soon will [Dm]sound!
[G7/F]O [C/E]sinner, [Am]hear the [Em/B]warning!
[Dm]To [A/C#]Jesus [C]quickly!
[C7/A#]Then [F/A]you, in [Am]that blest [C/G]morning,
[C/G]May [G7]meet Him in the [C]sky!
